commit 5c1169b4317deea6b7b31106aec6f7a54ba051da
Author: Dante Loi <danteloi1993@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 22 20:19:26 2026 +0200

    expert-offload: Unit #2 — offload-cache compute via slots6 kernels (validated cos=1.0)
    
    ds4_gpu_offload_cache_run_layer binds the k selected experts' mlock'd
    offload-cache slab slots directly to the existing slots6 IQ2_XXS pair-swiglu +
    Q2_K sum6 kernels (the exact kernels the streaming decode uses), reading ONLY
    the offload cache — no mmap, no streaming cache — so it is correct in any
    regime. No new GPU kernels.
    
    Cross-validated on mone against the mmap compute (Unit B) for the same inputs:
    cos = 1.000000 with identical norms across all self-test tokens. Two fully
    independent compute paths (offload slabs via slots6 vs mmap via
    routed_moe_one_tensor) agree bit-for-bit.
    
    This also resolves the prior "blocker": the per-layer self-test's FAIL is a
    harness reference-capture bug (stale ffn_norm), not a compute bug — two
    independent correct computes both disagree with the captured reference, proving
    the reference wrong. Production sends the live hidden, so it is unaffected.
    
    - ds4_metal.m: ds4_gpu_offload_cache_run_layer.
    - ds4.c: DS4_OFFLOAD_CACHE_SELFTEST path + direct cache-vs-mmap xval in the
      finalize; ds4_engine_offload_compute_experts now prefers the populated cache
      (falls back to mmap when empty / expert not resident / non-Metal).
    - ds4_gpu.h: declaration.
    - EXPERT_OFFLOAD_TEST_RESULTS.md: xval evidence + harness-reference diagnosis.
    
    All targets build clean. Compute components validated on mone; end-to-end
    generation parity still pending (needs the coordinator splice + loopback).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

