    expert-offload: root-cause the Unit-B self-test FAIL + clarify LRU in the plan
    
    Investigation on mone (model in SSD-streaming): the offload worker compute
    (ds4_gpu_offload_run_layer, which reuses the streaming-coupled
    routed_moe_one_tensor) produces output ORTHOGONAL to the decode reference
    (cos ~ 0), not a scaled/shifted version. Root cause: in --ssd-streaming the
    routed experts live only in the streaming slab cache (confirmed: forcing the
    mmap path fails with "model range not covered by mapped views"), and that cache
    is not reliably populated for the selected experts at the standalone worker /
    post-generation call site -> the compute reads the wrong expert weights.
    Loading the experts first (begin_selected_load, then the synchronous
    seed_selected) had zero effect, confirming the streaming path is the wrong
    foundation for the offload worker.
    
    Conclusion: the offload compute must read from the populated offload cache
    (g_offload_expert_cache_*, mlock'd, regime-independent) via the existing slots6
    IQ2/Q2_K kernels (Unit #2), not via the streaming-coupled path.
    
    - ds4.c: DS4_OFFLOAD_SELFTEST_DEBUG cosine/norm diagnostic in the finalize.
    - ds4_metal.m: offload_run_layer reverted to baseline + a NOTE documenting why
      the streaming-reuse path is wrong for offload.
    - DISTRIBUTED_EXPERT_OFFLOAD_PLAN.md: clarify the LRU intent (separate mlock'd
      offload cache reusing the LRU *policy*, not the streaming cache instance).
    - EXPERT_OFFLOAD_TEST_RESULTS.md: full evidence table + ruled-out experiments.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

